217 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(1.1 Purpose)/Pg 10 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

218 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(The purpose of this document is to provide a detailed Software Requirements Specification \(SRS\) for the Digital Notes Management System. This document describes the system\220s goals, users, features, constraints, and required functionalities to ensure a clear understanding among all stakeholders.)/Pg 10 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

219 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(1.2 Scope)/Pg 10 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

220 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(The Digital Notes Management System enables users\204including students, teachers, and professionals\204to create, categorize, store, search, and manage digital notes efficiently. The system supports tagging, cloud backup, and real-time collaborative editing. It targets individuals and teams who require an organized and centralized method for managing digital notes.)/Pg 10 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

221 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(1.3 Document Structure)/Pg 10 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

222 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(This document is organized into several sections to clearly define the requirements of the Digital Notes Management System.)/Pg 10 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

223 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1134 0 R/E(Section 1 provides the introduction, purpose, scope, document structure, constraints, key definitions ,overview and References )/Pg 10 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

224 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1135 0 R/E(Section 2 presents an overview of the system and its main capabilities.)/Pg 10 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

225 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1136 0 R/E(Section 3 describes the requirements engineering process, including gathering, analysis, and validation.)/Pg 10 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

226 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1137 0 R/E(Section 4 outlines the functional requirements of the system.)/Pg 10 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

227 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1138 0 R/E(Section 5 lists the non-functional requirements.)/Pg 10 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj

228 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1139 0 R/E(Section 6 describes the external interface requirements.)/Pg 10 0 R/K[12]>>
endobj

229 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1140 0 R/E(Section 7 presents the UML Use Case diagram.)/Pg 10 0 R/K[13]>>
endobj

230 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1141 0 R/E(Section 8 discusses ethical and professional responsibilities followed during development.)/Pg 10 0 R/K[14]>>
endobj

231 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(1.4 Constraints)/Pg 10 0 R/K[15]>>
endobj

232 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(The requirements engineering process for this system is affected by several constraints:)/Pg 10 0 R/K[16]>>
endobj

233 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1142 0 R/E(Time Constraints: The project must be completed within the academic semester, limiting the depth of requirements exploration.)/Pg 10 0 R/K[17]>>
endobj

234 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1143 0 R/E(Knowledge Constraints: Team members have varying levels of experience in software engineering, which may influence the complexity of the system.)/Pg 10 0 R/K[18]>>
endobj

235 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1144 0 R/E(Tool Limitations: The system design and diagrams must be created using approved tools \(Canva, Lucidchart, StarUML\), which may limit certain advanced modeling features.)/Pg 10 0 R/K[19]>>
endobj

236 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1145 0 R/E(Scope Limitations: The project focuses on analysis and design rather than full implementation, so requirements are defined at a conceptual level.)/Pg 10 0 R/K[20]>>
endobj

237 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1146 0 R/E(Resource Constraints: No actual server or cloud platform will be deployed; therefore, cloud-related requirements are documented hypothetically.)/Pg 10 0 R/K[21]>>
endobj

