256 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(2.1 Product Perspective)/Pg 12 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

257 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(The Digital Notes Management System is an independent software platform designed to help users create, organize, and manage digital notes. It operates as a standalone web or mobile application but may integrate with external services such as cloud storage providers for synchronization.)/Pg 12 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

258 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(The system is conceptually similar to existing note-taking tools like Notion, Evernote, and Google Keep, but with a stronger focus on structured tagging, collaboration, and academic productivity. It includes internal components such as:)/Pg 12 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

