endobj

698 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 167 0 R/Pg 36 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

699 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(In a digital notes management system, a user accesses the application to perform a variety of note-related operations. A user may create an account or log in if an account already exists. After successful authentication, the user is allowed to create new notes, edit existing notes, delete notes, search for notes, or share them with other users. Each operation triggers corresponding system functions such as saving, updating, retrieving, or applying sharing permissions.)/Pg 36 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

700 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/E(An administrator may also access the system to manage user accounts, review note records, or handle support requests. The system authenticates the administrator before allowing administrative actions. Both users and administrators may log out after completing their activities.)/Pg 36 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

